# Merchant Dashboard – Profile & Account (UI-Only) – Cursor Rule

## Objective
Design and implement the Merchant Profile & Account UI at `/profile` using Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and shadcn/ui. No backend or API calls. All data is mocked and stored client-side. Deliver an accessible, polished, and navigable page with tabs for:
- Business Information
- Account Settings
- Notification Preferences
- API Keys & Integrations

## Tech & Standards
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript
- UI: shadcn/ui
- Styling: Tailwind CSS only
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod
- State: Local component state (and optional Zustand for local-only persistence)
- Transitions: Follow Premium Transitions Rule; subtle, accessible animations
- Accessibility: Keyboard navigable, ARIA, color contrast, reduced motion support
- No Shopify UI or logic in this phase

## Routes
- `/profile` → Primary page with tabs and sub-sections
- All navigation is client-side; use `router.push('/dashboard')` for back

## Navigation & Layout
- Page header: back button, page title “Profile & Account”, short description
- Tabs (shadcn/ui `Tabs`): 
  - `business`
  - `settings`
  - `notifications`
  - `api`
- Each tab is a Card layout with semantic sections, forms, and primary/secondary actions

## Data & Validation (Zod)
Define schemas to validate and mock UI fields:
- BusinessInfoSchema:
  - business_name: string().min(2)
  - contactName: string().min(2)
  - email: string().email()
  - phone: string().min(7)
  - addressLine1: string().min(2)
  - addressLine2: string().optional()
  - city: string().min(2)
  - state: string().min(2)
  - zip: string().min(3)
  - country: string().min(2)
- AccountSettingsSchema:
  - language: enum(['en', 'fr'])
  - timezone: string().min(2)
  - dateFormat: enum(['MM/DD/YYYY', 'DD/MM/YYYY', 'YYYY-MM-DD'])
  - twoFactorEnabled: boolean()
- NotificationPrefsSchema:
  - emailUpdates: boolean()
  - smsUpdates: boolean()
  - pushUpdates: boolean()
  - deliveryAlerts: boolean()
  - weeklySummary: boolean()
- ApiKeysSchema:
  - primaryKey: string()
  - sandboxKey: string()
  - webhookUrl: string().url().optional()
  - ipAllowlist: array(string()).optional()

Mock data is loaded on mount and saved to `localStorage` on submit. No server calls.

## Event Handling
- Use const handlers: `const handleSubmitBusiness = () => {}`, etc.
- Show success/error toasts on Save/Reset
- Early returns for invalid state or disabled actions
- Keep handlers pure; no side-effects outside UI/localStorage

## Accessibility
- All actionable elements: `aria-label`, focus states, and keyboard handlers
- Tabs must be keyboard navigable and labeled
- Inputs with associated `Label` and `aria-describedby` for errors
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable non-essential motion

## Premium Transitions
- Apply subtle hover/focus transitions using `transition-all duration-200 ease-[var(--easing-smooth)]`
- On active: `scale-95` for tactile feedback (avoid `translateY(-2px)` on hover by default)
- Animate entrance with fade/slide (opacity/transform only)
- Provide reduced motion guard

## Naming & IDs
- Use project prefix `parcego-` for IDs
- Examples:
  - `parcego-profile-back-btn`
  - `parcego-profile-tabs`
  - `parcego-profile-business-form`
- Ensure IDs are globally unique

## UI Structure (per tab)

### Business Information
- Fields: Business/Contact names, Email, Phone, Address (L1, L2), City, State, Zip, Country
- Actions: Save changes, Reset
- Display a compact summary card header with avatar and merchant name

### Account Settings
- Fields: Language, Timezone, Date format, Toggle 2FA (UI-only)
- Actions: Save changes, Reset

### Notification Preferences
- Toggles: Email, SMS, Push, Delivery Alerts, Weekly Summary
- Actions: Save changes, Reset

### API Keys & Integrations
- Show masked keys with copy buttons
- Regenerate (UI-only; confirm dialog)
- Webhook URL input, IP allowlist multiline input (comma or newline separated)
- Actions: Save changes, Reset

## Pseudocode – Implementation Plan
1. Create `/profile` page with header:
   - Back button → `/dashboard`
   - Title, description
2. Add `Tabs` with values: business, settings, notifications, api
3. For each tab:
   - Wrap content in `Card`
   - Build `Form` using RHF + Zod resolver
   - Preload mock data from `localStorage` (fallback to seeded defaults)
   - On Save:
     - Validate with Zod
     - Save to `localStorage`
     - Show success toast
   - On Reset:
     - Restore defaults
     - Show neutral toast
4. Accessibility:
   - Proper `aria-*` on tabs, forms, buttons
   - Label every input
   - Keyboard support (Enter to submit; Esc to cancel where relevant)
5. Transitions:
   - Fade-in page container